# 7. INVENTORY MANAGEMENT MODULE

Implement proper inventory tracking.

Inventory fields:
- Inventory ID
- Product ID
- Quantity On Hand
- Reserved Quantity
- Available Quantity
- Minimum Stock Level
- Last Updated

Formula:

Available Quantity = Quantity On Hand - Reserved Quantity

Features:
- View all inventory.
- Search products.
- Filter low-stock products.
- Track stock availability.
- View stock movement history.
- Record stock additions.
- Record manual stock adjustments with reasons.
- Display low-stock alerts.
- Maintain inventory transaction history.

Inventory transaction types:
- STOCK_IN
- STOCK_ADJUSTMENT
- STOCK_RESERVED
- STOCK_RELEASED
- STOCK_DEDUCTED

Every stock change must be recorded with:
- Product ID
- Transaction type
- Quantity
- Reference order ID (when applicable)
- Previous quantity
- New quantity
- User who performed the action
- Reason
- Timestamp

Never allow negative inventory.

Use database locking or atomic updates to prevent concurrent orders from overselling stock.

